{"id":"elements-crust","title":"Most abundant elements in Earth's crust","prompt":"Name the 10 chemical elements that make up the most of Earth's crust (by mass)","noun":"elements","category":"Science","metric":"Share of the crust by mass","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: Abundance of elements in Earth's crust","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abundance_of_elements_in_Earth's_crust","asOf":"2026-11-20"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Oxygen","aliases":["Element 8","Oxygyn","Diatomic Oxygen","Dephlogisticated air","Vital air","E948","Active oxygen","Oxygen rings","Pure oxygen","Oxygen gas","Oxygen atom","Atomic number 8","Oxigen","Oxygen ion","Oxygen, 8O","Nitroaereus","Medical oxygen","Oxygen applications","Oxygen uses","O=O","O2"],"value":"46.1%","n":461000,"article":"Oxygen","fact":{"text":"No one person discovered it: Scheele found it in 1773 or earlier, Priestley in 1774.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxygen"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Silicon","aliases":["Si","Silisium","Silicium","Silicis","Silicon crystalization","Metallurgical grade silicon","Semiconducting silicon","Refined silicon","Silocon","Element 14","Biological silicon","Silicon production","Silicon alloys","14Si","Silicon applications","Silicon uses","Silcon"],"value":"28.2%","n":282000,"article":"Silicon","fact":{"text":"Humphry Davy named it silicium, from silex (flint); Thomas Thomson renamed it silicon in 1817.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silicon"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Aluminium","aliases":["Al","Element 13","Super Purity Aluminium","Aluminium substratum","Alluminum","Super purity aluminum","Alumium","E173","Aluminium production","Alumnium","Alumino","Billeted aluminum","Billet aluminium","Aluminum","Aliuminium","Cast aluminium","Aluminun","Cast aluminum","13Al","Aluminium applications","Aluminium uses","Aluminum applications","Aluminum uses","Aluminum salt","Aluminium salt","Aluminum production","Aluminuum"],"value":"8.23%","n":82300,"article":"Aluminium","fact":{"text"